<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90768" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προ-χοή</span></b>  (A), ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προχέω</span>) poet. noun, almost always pl., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>outpouring</i>, i.e.
			<i>mouth</i>, of a river, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ προχοῇσι διιπετέος ποταμοῖο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					17.263
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς ποταμοῦ προχοάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.453
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν προχοῇς ποταμοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.242
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν προχοῇς . . Ὠκεανοῖο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					20.65
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τριτωνίδος ἐν προχοαῖς λίμνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.20
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Anacr.
				28
			</span></i> codd., <i><span class="en">
				B.
				6.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				1025
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				272
			</span></i>, Theoc.Chius in <i><span class="en">
				<u>FHG</u>
				 ii 86
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				480
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θερμαῖς ὕδατος μαλακοῦ
			π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				192.8
			</span></i> (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδατος προχοὰς χειμερίους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.147
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Antag.
			</span></i>): sg. is dub. l. in <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				757
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προχοὴ τῶν ὑδάτων</span>
			<i>discharge</i> of amniotic fluid, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cat.Cod.Astr.</u>
				8(4).127
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>overflow, flood</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.271
			</span></i> (pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόχωσις</span>
			, <i>promontory</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Archestr.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				40
			</span></i> codd.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
			</span></i> (sed leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προβολαῖσι</span>).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>libations,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				14.1595
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Marc.</u>
				23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				312.16
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Smyrna</span>).</div>
